From: PocketBoot developers <noreply@pocketboot.org>
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] arm64: dts: qcom: tbx304x: include APQ8017 selection ID

The Wi-Fi TB-X304F reports soc_id 307 (APQ8017) and board-id
<0x1000b 0>. Retain the family compatible and MSM8917 ID from the board
port, adding only the verified APQ8017 ID. This is bootloader selection
metadata, not a claim that every peripheral on the F variant is validated.

Base: pem120/linux-msm89x7 a51b91b503307d35902447dd1f90db765372cf3b

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917-lenovo-tbx304x.dts
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 	compatible = "lenovo,tbx304x", "qcom,msm8917";
 	model = "Lenovo Tab 4 10 (tbx304x)";
 	qcom,board-id = <0x1000b 0>;
-	qcom,msm-id = <QCOM_ID_MSM8917 0>;
+	qcom,msm-id = <QCOM_ID_MSM8917 0>, <QCOM_ID_APQ8017 0>;
 
 	aliases {
 		mmc0 = &sdhc_1;
